From cb5aeb0b277b7e150135043b2950e046ef6eaad7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luissalet <luismasc16@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 02:19:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/36] Make the server's launch choices one named profile with
 a hash
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ControlNet, the LoRA folder, the upscalers folder, memory placement and
flash attention are all command-line arguments. No request can change
one, so the set of them is the identity of the running process exactly
as the loaded model is, and changing any of them costs the same restart.

That was already true and only partly acted on: ensureSdServer compared
the model, the LoRA folder and the ControlNet by hand, and did not
compare the upscalers folder at all. So an ESRGAN installed while the
server was up did not get --hires-upscalers-dir until something
unrelated happened to restart it, and a hires pass naming that model was
refused in the meantime.

One SdRuntimeProfile now carries all six, launchProfile is the single
place that decides what a launch looks like, and both spawnServer and
ensureSdServer go through it — so "what flags do we start with" and
"does this job need a restart" are literally the same computation and
cannot drift apart. This generalises the model-switch logic rather than
adding a second path beside it.

sdProfileRestartReasons exists so the price can be shown before it is
paid. A writer who ticks a checkbox and waits forty seconds with no
explanation concludes the app is broken; one who is told the change
reloads the model waits happily. The profile and its hash ride on
SdRuntimeStatus for the studio to compare against.

